  "articleBody": "Thinking about tiling your basement? That's a great idea for durability and style! But before you pick out your favorite tiles, it's super important to check if your basement slab is actually ready for them. A common question we get is whether the slab is flat enough. You really don't want more than a quarter-inch variation over a 10-foot span. If it's not, you're setting yourself up for uneven tiles and future headaches. Another big one is moisture. Basements can be damp, and you absolutely need to know how much moisture is present before choosing your tile and adhesive system. Skipping these checks can lead to tiles lifting or cracking later on. Finally, think about how much extra tile to buy. Beyond just the square footage, you'll need about 10-15% extra for cuts, waste, and any future repairs. It's better to have a few extra on hand than to try to match a discontinued tile later. If you're unsure about any of these steps, especially with significant cracks or unevenness, a pro can really help ensure a smooth, lasting finish. We're here to help make your basement renovation a success!",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
